        "original_id": "1bac8b3e-ea91-5521-8b70-c3555c6a44ff",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1998 British Touring Car Championship\n- People: Rickard Rydell\n- Products: Volvo S40, Mitsubishi Carisma\n- Companies: Volvo Cars, Volvo, Mitsubishi\n- Places: Born, Netherlands\n- Organizations: NedCar factory\n\nFacts:\n- The Volvo S40 was marketed and produced by Volvo Cars from 1995 to 2012 across two generations.\n- The 1998 British Touring Car Championship was eventually won by Rickard Rydell in a Volvo S40 with a round to spare.\n- The Mitsubishi Carisma was co-developed with Volvo and shared its chassis with the first generation of the Volvo S40.\n- The Mitsubishi Carisma was built at the NedCar factory in Born, Netherlands, which Volvo and Mitsubishi co-owned at the time.",
